      "issue": 22,
      "title": "Floorplanning - Lesson 6",
      "status": "Done",
      "authors": [
        "Su3037"
      ],
      "issue_url": "https://github.com/yongfu-li/eda-learning/issues/22",
      "urls": [
        "https://github.com/Su3037/floorplanning-lesson6-sequence-pair",
        "https://su3037.github.io/floorplanning-lesson6-sequence-pair/",
        "https://claude.ai/code"
      ],
      "comments": [
        "Hi Prof. Li,\n\nLesson 6 (Sequence-Pair) is done as a standalone open-source lesson:\n\n- Repository: https://github.com/Su3037/floorplanning-lesson6-sequence-pair\n- Website: https://su3037.github.io/floorplanning-lesson6-sequence-pair/ (Chinese first; English edition at `/en/`)\n\nWhat it contains: a lesson page; an interactive lab where you edit pos/neg and step through every relation, constraint edge and longest-path maximum; four films (popular, concise, advanced, lab walkthrough) with Chinese and English captions; a 14-page deck (PDF and editable PPTX with notes); 7 graded challenges and 6 concept checks; an in-browser Python code lab and a downloadable Python pack. It uses your `common/pack.py` convention and the five-block example, and is credited under CC BY 4.0.\n\nAll numbers come from the engine and are tested: ABCED / DABCE gives a 9 × 4 packing with D at (0, 3); all 14,400 pairs are overlap-free and 13,680 fit the 10 × 8 outline; the JS engine is cross-checked against an independent Python reference.\n\nNote: `common/goldens.py`'s `GOLDEN_PACK` draws D at y = 2; that is a different illustration, not the packing of ABCED / DABCE, and the lesson says so.\n\nLimitations: fixed block sizes (rotation only as a labelled extension); no search/annealing beyond neighbour moves; the popular film's music is a third-party track used at the author's choice and is not covered by the repository's licences.\n\nThank you!\nSu3037\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n"
      ]
    },
